+        // longer owns the screen - resume vanilla dead-player scoreboard behaviour for
+        // whatever remains of this death, exactly as if squadenter() had never suppressed
+        // it above. Guarded on player1->state==CS_DEAD: several of this function's callers
+        // (squadupdate()'s abort poll, above) fire AFTER the player has already left
+        // CS_DEAD - respawn confirmed, entered edit mode, entered spectator - and each of
+        // those transitions already calls showscores(false) itself at the point it
+        // happens, so re-showing the scoreboard here would be a regression, not a restore.
